      "value": "@{674242fab51f51daae5cedc8|full_name}, the access isn't the issue for me, and that's just my opinion and experience with an older computer you read. I have good internet and an SD Card to offload games onto. You read too deeply into my side story. There are ways to clear cached worlds, both with and without using/launching VRChat itself, anyway. \n\nMy main point I wanted to point out was that you can compress assets to help with the current PC World Size limitation.\n\nI gave some tips at the end about considering adding compression at the end for world creation, to help with the current storage cap. \n\nIf they do decide to make the cap larger, I would like the cap to be increased for Mobile/Standalone Platforms, too, if possible.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
